# The CoreVue reporting UI is compiled to ES2015 (Vite/esbuild `target: es2015`), and Vue 3
# itself requires native ES2015 support - including Proxy, which cannot be polyfilled. A browser
# without full native ES2015 therefore cannot run the compiled UI at all, no matter which
# polyfills we ship, so there is no point targeting anything older here. This list is only used
# to decide which core-js polyfills the shared CoreVue polyfill bundle needs; the versions below
# are the first releases with complete native ES2015 support in each engine.
chrome >= 51
edge >= 15
firefox >= 54
safari >= 10
ios_saf >= 10
opera >= 38
samsung >= 5
not dead
